# Summary
Introduced a low-severity information disclosure by moving object-lock configuration validation ahead of authorization checks.
In lock_object_for_authorized_object_lock the code now calls ensure_object_lock_bucket (which returns an InvalidRequest error when Object Lock is disabled) before it evaluates bucket-policy authorization. This means an unauthenticated or unauthorized requester can probe Get/Put ObjectRetention or LegalHold and observe a different error for buckets without Object Lock enabled, leaking configuration state that previously returned AccessDenied. The pre-commit path authorized the requester first, preventing this disclosure.

